age":100.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-19.205951712521056,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":100.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.05046908906981677,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":44.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.3207879165364407,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":22.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.03451216572610354,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":56.9,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.11269120662090604,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.030625898419213773,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":26.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.07262260003554948,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":9.1,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.4700690511302297,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.016525873910649087,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":33.5,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0018837901037061114,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":13.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.037385063670744234,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":3.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07367899627756315,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.23796,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Grid Dynamics Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides enterprise artificial intelligence and digital transformation services in North America, Europe, and internationally. The company offers artificial intelligence services, such as AI-Readiness through strategy consulting, data modernization, rapid and deployment-ready prototyping, and software development lifecycle transformation; identify AI use cases service, which deploys AI in customer-facing, operational, and knowledge management scenarios; AI infrastructure agentic systems; and enterprise AI scale, which helps enterprises gain enterprise-wide efficiency with deployment. It also provides cloud platform and product engineering services, including digital engagement, which delivers modular composable commerce platforms; IoT and edge computing, which assists manufacturers and logistics providers in implementing physical AI; and AI and data platforms. The company serves retail, technology, media and telecom, finance, consumer packaged goods and manufacturing, healthcare and pharma, and other verticals. Grid Dynamics Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in San Ramon, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Leonard  Livschitz | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $90K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 30%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 18\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Grid Dynamics Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.1B market cap on $412M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $25M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 24% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 69% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6939813441523974},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Amadeus IT Group (OTCMKTS:AMADY) & Grid Dynamics (NASDAQ:GDYN) Financial Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/amadeus-it-group-otcmktsamady-grid-dynamics-nasdaqgdyn-financial-survey.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576530.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.927,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Grid Dynamics Holdings, Inc. (GDYN) Hits Fresh High: Is There Still Room to Run?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028072/grid-dynamics-holdings-inc-gdyn-hits-fresh-high-is-there-still-room-to-run?cid=CS-ZC-FT-52_week_high-3028072","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794427560.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Grid Dynamics Holdings Inc. (GDYN) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/How_Grid_Dynamics_Holdings_Inc._GDYN_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111126123802_1794418682.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794418682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Leonard Livschitz to Sell 20,000 Shares of Grid Dynamics Holdings (GDYN) via Form 144 Filing","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/leonard-livschitz-to-sell-20000-shares-of-grid-dynamics-holdings-gdyn-via-form-144-filing","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794362517